docs/dev/SPEC.md:3:## Scope and authority
docs/dev/SPEC.md:7:R-001 through R-013 specify the intended initial two-phase system; milestone labels identify delivery obligations without authorizing implementation. F-001 through F-004 retain the later separately requested range feature's contract as a deferred compatibility constraint. That feature is outside the initial executable hierarchy. No focused specification children are needed.
docs/dev/SPEC.md:9:## Public API and values
docs/dev/SPEC.md:11:### R-001 Direct exports and statistics
docs/dev/SPEC.md:15:### R-002 Whole-input counting API
docs/dev/SPEC.md:19:### R-003 Line semantics
docs/dev/SPEC.md:23:### R-004 Word semantics
docs/dev/SPEC.md:27:### R-005 BOM policy
docs/dev/SPEC.md:31:### R-006 Named-file decode, failure and ownership
docs/dev/SPEC.md:35:## CLI contracts
docs/dev/SPEC.md:37:### R-007 Baseline named-file invocation
docs/dev/SPEC.md:43:### R-008 CLI failures and usage
docs/dev/SPEC.md:47:### R-009 JSON output
docs/dev/SPEC.md:49:Phase 2 milestone 2.1 supplies `--json`, composing with `--keep-bom` and named-file input. Success returns 0 with one JSON object and a final newline, empty stderr, and exactly the keys `lines` and `words`, each containing an integer equal to the text-format count. No extra fields or JSON booleans are permitted. Key order and spacing are unrestricted. Without `--json`, preserve R-007 text output. Failures retain R-008, regardless of output selection.
docs/dev/SPEC.md:51:### R-010 Stdin input
docs/dev/SPEC.md:53:Phase 2 milestone 2.2 supplies input token `-` as stdin. Read bytes until EOF and decode complete content as strict UTF-8 independently of locale, without closing stdin. Apply the same counting/BOM/output policies as named files. Empty stdin returns (0, 0). Read or decode failure returns 1, identifies stdin and the cause on stderr, and produces empty stdout with no traceback. Stdin acquisition does not alter `count_file` semantics or add an API export. Output succeeds only after complete input acquisition and decoding.
docs/dev/SPEC.md:55:## Documentation, testing and distribution
docs/dev/SPEC.md:57:### R-011 Public documentation and runnable README
docs/dev/SPEC.md:59:Phase 1 milestone 1.2 supplies public API/module documentation describing exports/signatures, counts, BOM policy, silent APIs, strict decoding, exceptions and handle ownership. The README supplies runnable named-file/module-entry examples, setup and test instructions, output/status/help behavior and distribution usage. Phase 2 final exits update documentation for JSON/stdin and retained behavior. Documentation must describe delivered capabilities accurately; the preparation README's present lack of runnable code is explicit until delivery.
docs/dev/SPEC.md:61:### R-012 Product verification organization
docs/dev/SPEC.md:65:### R-013 Extracted-source distribution
docs/dev/SPEC.md:69:## Deferred range feature
docs/dev/SPEC.md:71:### F-001 Range grammar and validation
docs/dev/SPEC.md:75:### F-002 Selection semantics and decode ordering
docs/dev/SPEC.md:79:### F-003 Composition and delivery boundary
docs/dev/SPEC.md:83:### F-004 Objective range acceptance
docs/dev/SPEC.md:98:## Whole-input acceptance matrix
docs/dev/SPEC.md:119:Named-file and text API results agree for these inputs. CLI text and JSON agree where delivered. Verify non-ASCII UTF-8, CRLF boundaries, owned-handle closure after decode/read failures, immutable results and unchanged input bytes. CLI integration covers named-file paths (including dash-prefixed), help, missing/extra inputs, unknown options, missing/unreadable/read-failing files, bad bytes, empty stdout on failures and useful diagnostics. Phase 2 adds text/JSON stdin, empty stdin, invalid bytes/read errors, locale independence and retained stream ownership. Distribution acceptance repeats the appropriate delivered module-entry behaviors after extraction.
docs/dev/SPEC.md:121:## Behavioral ownership and review boundary
docs/dev/SPEC.md:127:| R-006/R-010 | C-005 acquisition, C-006 API and C-008 CLI |
docs/dev/SPEC.md:129:| R-011/R-012/R-013 | Public boundaries C-001 through C-009, supported by documentation and product/distribution verification |
docs/dev/SPEC.md:130:| F-001 through F-004 | C-007/C-008 and deferred C-010 over C-002/C-003/C-004; no additional API export |
docs/dev/TASKS.md:3:## Governing inputs and execution boundary
docs/dev/TASKS.md:5:This complete initial two-phase hierarchy derives from accepted [PROJECT](PROJECT.md), [ARCHITECTURE](ARCHITECTURE.md), [DECOMPOSITION](DECOMPOSITION.md), [SPEC](SPEC.md), [PLAN](PLAN.md) and [layout](layout.md), with current [SPEC QC](SPEC-REVIEW-REPORT.md) and [combined PLAN QC](PLAN-REVIEW-REPORT.md). There is no pre-existing product task list or verified implementation; all checkboxes are unchecked. Monotonic project-wide IDs T-001 through T-017 are allocated here once and have exactly one executable owner.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:7:Task details identify outcomes, likely edit scopes, prerequisite IDs and objective evidence. Each task includes its own relevant tests/docstrings/docs rather than separate padding work. The phase/milestone names match PLAN. Deferred SPEC F-001 through F-004/C-010 have no implementation task or hosted issue in this hierarchy; preserve their design seams while implementing accepted whole-input capabilities.
