docs/dev/TASKS.md:110:## Completion and persistence rules
docs/dev/TASKS.md:118:## T-001 completion evidence
docs/dev/TASKS.md:120:The current request supersedes the historical preparation-only stopping statements for exactly the first executable Phase 1 task. Selected T-001 in milestone 1.1, with no task dependency. Accepted preparation tip `1e3305c8659045945244c06861079fef879ca3c3` was explicitly merged into actual default `main`, parent `eff696b38f0b8a94bd6f91ca1c64d54fd714df46`, as `88a5c4b4424f4bba76940e40b1d6523b1f6fe191`; merged document hashes, local links, heading spacing and document-only scope were verified and that exact remote tip read back before creating `phase/1-named-file-utility` from it. The accepted disclosure's two pre-existing whitespace warnings were preserved.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:122:Maintained Phase 1 tracking is confirmed by the current request. Before task edits/tests, provider readback verified `sdd-phase-1-Named-file-utility`, native milestones 1–3 (1.1, 1.2, 1.3), and unique marked T-001 through T-009 issues 2–10 with their phase label and correct milestone association. T-001 uniquely maps to `pchemguy/SDD-Manager-Prerelease-Playground#2`, milestone 1. Existing unrelated labels, issue text/comments and milestone content are preserved; later phases remain unprojected.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:128:After implementing the contracts, `python -m unittest discover -s tests/unit -t . -v` passed all 10 tests and `python -m unittest discover -s tests/integration -t . -v` passed all 5 tests, without skips or warnings. Evidence covers every whole-input SPEC matrix row under both policies; Unicode separators/whitespace and non-ASCII words; mixed/consecutive/final terminators; repeated/interior BOMs; equality, invalid fields and assignment/deletion immutability; direct exports/signatures, keyword-only policy, repeated-call independence and import/call silence. Verification also inspects source/document contracts and preserved internal segment seams. Coverage is T-001 on this runtime, not full Python-version, file/API, CLI or distribution acceptance. The future check tools are absent because their owning tasks are unselected.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:130:Exactly T-001's result, tests, documentation, current evidence and initial checkbox close together in its task commit. Publication and issue closure are subsequent observed operations reported in the workflow handoff. All parents and T-002 through T-017 remain unchecked. Stop after the verified push and hosted reconciliation of T-001; do not integrate the incomplete phase or start another task.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:132:## T-002 completion evidence
docs/dev/TASKS.md:134:The milestone 1.1 request selects T-002 through T-004 and supersedes historical first-task/preparation stops only within this boundary. Startup clean branch/remote tip was `9dc8075dd1b96d3a2744717a9d6d98a3024acbec`; its T-001 result/evidence/initial checkbox and single-ID subject were inspected and compliant. Accepted preparation remains published on main `88a5c4b4424f4bba76940e40b1d6523b1f6fe191`. Current SPEC/PLAN/layout and adjacent Ready owner reviews retain unchanged governing contracts; TASKS differs only in T-001 completion evidence/status, which does not invalidate hierarchy QC. Maintained phase tracking readback returned the phase label, milestones 1–3 and unique marked T-001–T-009 issues 2–10 with correct parent associations before task edits/tests. T-002 maps uniquely to issue #3, milestone #1; T-001 issue #2 is closed.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:140:## T-003 completion evidence
docs/dev/TASKS.md:142:T-002 was closed durably at `f28f6e415b3e0c13353a61e82354c47b0d2cabb2`, pushed and read back as exact remote phase tip before T-003 work. Provider readback confirms its issue #3 closed/completed with the evidence comment; recovery after an overbroad Link-header guard independently read actual closed state and the existing comment without duplicating writes. T-003 uniquely maps to maintained issue #4, milestone #1.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:148:Real module processes verify named UTF-8/mixed terminator/Unicode/BOM/empty input, exact status/stdout/stderr, before/after BOM option order, help without input, required single input and actual dash-prefixed names after `--`, including a file named `--keep-bom` and literal `-`. API equality and unchanged bytes are checked. Controlled CLI seams assert default/retaining policy and help without acquisition. Source/docstring/staged-scope review found no current contract violation. Complete R-008 diagnostics/status robustness, standalone public docs/distribution, JSON/stdin/range and other runtimes remain outside this task. The named-file useful demonstration and coherent milestone review follow in T-004; milestone/phase remain unchecked here.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:150:## T-004 completion evidence
docs/dev/TASKS.md:152:Completed the separate coherent milestone implementation code review, actual nonempty runner, API/module demonstration and exit assessment in [milestone 1.1 report](reports/phases/1/1.1.md), reviewed at published T-003 source `373203d6f41bee2229eed900b761de8669678e0b`. The runner passed 21 unit and 12 integration tests on Python 3.12.14, with no skips/warnings. Mixed-terminator/non-ASCII/BOM temporary-file API and real CLI returned three lines/four words with exact streams/status and unchanged bytes; BOM-only default versus retaining calls visibly produced zero/zero versus one/one. Source review found no milestone contract blocker and no required repair; TODO is None. Full runtime/platform matrix, complete CLI failure diagnostics, public guide/distribution and later phase capabilities remain unverified/planned in their owning tasks.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:154:T-002/T-003 separate closing commits were inspected and published before this review; provider readback confirms issues #3/#4 closed/completed with evidence, and T-001 #2 remains closed. Unique T-004 issue is #5 in native milestone #1. The report/evidence, initial T-004 checkbox and eligible milestone 1.1 parent close together; phase and unselected tasks remain unchecked. Publish/read back this task commit before closing issue #5, then validate all milestone-associated task issues and close/read back milestone #1. Stop on the incomplete phase branch, with main unchanged and no release or T-005 work.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:156:## T-005 completion evidence
docs/dev/TASKS.md:158:The complete-phase request selects T-005 through T-009 and explicit full-phase integration, superseding the historical Phase 1 partial stops. Startup published phase tip `7d003c1cf31c994340d8644e95990ef2253754ed` and main `88a5c4b4424f4bba76940e40b1d6523b1f6fe191` were read back exactly; latest T-004 closing result/report/evidence/initial checkbox composition is compliant. Current SPEC/PLAN/layout hashes match the accepted Ready owner reports, and TASKS changes only completion/evidence, preserving reviewed hierarchy/contracts. Provider readback verified all nine uniquely marked Phase 1 task issues #2–#10 with phase label and milestones #1–#3, and T-001–T-004 issues plus milestone #1 closed. T-005 uniquely maps to #6 in milestone #2; unrelated hosted material is retained.
docs/dev/TASKS.md:162:`python tools/check_tests.py` passed 23 unit and 14 integration tests on Python 3.12.14, no skips/warnings; `git diff --check` passed. Controlled open/read/decode/owned-handle checks and CLI failures, real subprocess missing/bad-byte inputs under both BOM policies, invocation errors before acquisition, exact success/help streams, API semantics and unchanged bytes are covered. Source/docstring inspection found no scoped contract blocker. Broader runtime/platform coverage, public guide and distribution remain later selected tasks; Phase 2 stays unselected. Result/tests/source documentation/current evidence and initial T-005 checkbox close together before publication and issue #6 reconciliation.
